    <briefdescription>
<para>A container for an operand bundle being viewed as a set of values rather than a set of uses. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Unlike <ref refid="structllvm_1_1_operand_bundle_use" kindref="compound">OperandBundleUse</ref>, <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_operand_bundle_def_t" kindref="compound">OperandBundleDefT</ref> owns the memory it carries, and so it is possible to create and pass around &quot;self-contained&quot; instances of <ref refid="namespacellvm_1aa97c65466bdd34abda6772dd32eb5d19" kindref="member">OperandBundleDef</ref> and <ref refid="namespacellvm_1af4f524db4940157ee7b5f8fac25d11f5" kindref="member">ConstOperandBundleDef</ref>. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
